 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Family and grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "BC546 is the high-voltage member, rated 65 V collector to emitter and 80 V collector to base. BC547 and BC550 are rated 45 V and 50 V, BC548 and BC549 30 V for both. BC549 and BC550 are the low-noise members, with noise-figure limits of 4.0 dB or less against 10.0 dB for the others. hFE at VCE = 5 V, IC = 2 mA is graded in classes A (110 to 220), B (200 to 450) and C (420 to 800); the class letter ends the marking, as in BC547B."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Complementary types",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "BC556, BC557, BC558, BC559 and BC560 are the matching PNP transistors. All devices are lead-free."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain and saturation over current",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Typical gain stays near 200 from 1 mA to about 30 mA and falls to about 60 at 300 mA. With base current one tenth of collector current, VCE(sat) is about 40 mV below 5 mA and rises to about 400 mV at 300 mA, while VBE(sat) runs from about 690 mV to 1 V. fT peaks near 360 MHz at around 27 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Availability",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Nine ordering codes are current: BC546ABU, BC546CTA, BC547BBU, BC547BTF, BC547CBU, BC547CTA, BC549BTA, BC549CTA and BC550CBU. Twelve further codes, including every BC548, are discontinued."
  }
 ],
